<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sancho García of Castile</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1017</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sancho García was count of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> from 995 to 1017. He fought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almanzor">Almanzor</a> and his sons and took advantage of the collapse of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">Caliphate</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a>, intervening in its civil war in 1009 and recovering frontier fortresses. He granted generous fueros to frontier settlers, earning the nickname 'of the good laws', and his daughter's marriage linked Castile to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-navarre">Navarre</a>.</p></div>
